.TH @PROG@ 1 "@PROJECT_YEAR@" "@PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
@PROG@, @COLON@ \- rsync with colon-path local names
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @COLON@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.I SRC
\&...
.I DEST
.br
.B @PROG@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B @PROG@
wraps
.BR rsync (1)
with colon-path rewriting for local
.B BASE:LEAF
arguments.
.I host:path
and
.I host::module
forms are not treated as colon-paths.
.PP
See
.BR colon-path (7).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show wrapper help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-colon\-dry\-run
Print the rewritten
.B rsync
command without executing it.
.PP
Other options are passed through to
.BR rsync (1).
See the original manual for the complete option set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rsync (1),
.BR colon-scp (1),
.BR colon-path (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by @PROJECT_AUTHOR@ <@PROJECT_EMAIL@>.
